  "description": "Operation records (T3): execute an authorized operation at most once. Each scenario runs against ONE fresh in-memory OperationStore and a fixed clock per step (`at`, epoch ms); `expect[i]` is the answer to `steps[i]`. `execute` takes a pre-authorized operation {id, verb, resource, params_digest} with a PCActn that carries `exp` and a signed reversibility class (`signed_class`), the server class, an optional recheck (ok / refuse with reason / throw with message), `recheck_for`, `timeout_ms`, and a function that commits `result` (default: the idempotency key), throws `message`, or re-enters the same execution; answers are {outcome, fn_calls, record}. Reason and error strings are compared exactly. `no_store` / `not_allowed` exercise the refusals.",
